{% doc %}
  Outputs the loading value for an image in the current section: 'eager' in the first three sections of
  the page (likely on the first screen, so the browser fetches them at once), 'lazy' further down (fetched
  only when the visitor scrolls near them).

  The one place for this rule: snippets/image.liquid, the hero and its blocks all use it, so the cut-off
  can't drift apart. Use it inside a capture, then strip the result: the captured text can start with a
  newline, and the browser treats loading="\nlazy" as an unknown value (= eager).

  @example
  {% capture image_loading %}{% render 'section-loading' %}{% endcapture %}
  {% assign image_loading = image_loading | strip %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  if section.index > 3
    echo 'lazy'
  else
    echo 'eager'
  endif
-%}
